#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An ArchiMate model is authored in Archi and committed; everything a reader sees is derived from it by three mechanical Tools, in order, in the pipeline lane: `archimate-check` (it parses and resolves), `archimate-metamodel` (the element types and relationship patterns it uses, each checked against ArchiMate's relationship table), and `archimate-pages` (a page and an IRI for every view, element and relationship, every view drawn, and the \"Metamodel in use\" page). No step draws a diagram by hand, and none runs Archi or a JVM (skill `archimate-models`). The metamodel is the second step's output, so it cannot disagree with the model."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the metamodel step's exit code: does every relationship follow a pattern ArchiMate's relationship table allows? `yes` publishes; `no` goes back to the author with the patterns and relationship ids it printed."
msgstr ""

