#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:61
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The author changes the relationship's type or ends in Archi and commits the model again. The pipeline never rewrites a model."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:25
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person who draws the model in Archi, on their own machine. A finding from the pipeline is theirs to act on: the pipeline never edits a model."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:44
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `archimate-check` (`archimate:validate`, on the instance root): every model the config names is held and parses, every box in every view draws an element the model holds, every relationship's ends are in the model."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:50
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `archimate-metamodel` (`archimate:metamodel --check`, on the instance root): the element types the model uses and every (source type, relationship, target type) pattern, each checked against ArchiMate's relationship table. Placeholder elements named after their own type are reported, never fatal: removing them is the author's call."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `archimate-pages` (`archimate:pages --out`, into the site being built): a JSON-LD node and a thin page for every view, element and relationship, every view drawn as SVG, and each model's \"Metamodel in use\" page with its diagram laid out from DOT by Graphviz in WebAssembly, plus the same diagram as DOT, Mermaid and JSON."
msgstr ""

